  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 215 AM Wednesday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... It will be drier and rather pleasant much of the \nweek, then increasing showers and thunderstorms over the weekend \ninto next week.  \n\nHigh pressure will shift from the Upper Mississippi Valley to \nover the Mid-Atlantic states by Friday. Expect to see temperatures \nto be slightly below normal for late July. As the high pressure \nshifts offshore over the weekend, expect increasing moisture and \nthunderstorm chances again by Saturday in the west and elsewhere by \nSunday into early next week.  This return of moisture with a trough \nlikely developing just west of the Appalachians will keep the \ntemperatures check Sunday into early next week. Highs may hold in \nthe 80s. Additional heavy rainfall is possible late in the weekend \ninto next week that may continue to bring relief with the ongoing \ndrought.",
